  "ocr_text": "SWORN BROTHERS (fratres jurati), perfons who, by mutual oath, covenanted to fhare each others fortune. Formerly, in any notable expedition to invade and conquer an enemy’s country, it was the cultom for the more eminent foldiers to engage themselves by reciprocal oaths to fhare the rewards of their service. This practice gave occasion to the proverb of feworn brothers or brethren in miquity, because of their dividing plunder and fpoil."
